# CODEOWNERS for FARO
#
# The `protect-def-branches` ruleset has `require_code_owner_review` enabled, so
# every path listed here requires approval from at least one of its owners
# before merging. Since a PR author cannot approve their own PR, having all
# three team members as owners guarantees there are always two possible
# reviewers for any change.
#
# All three members are owners on equal terms across the whole repository. The
# paths below do not restrict ownership. They are listed explicitly to mark
# where the impact of a mistake is highest and review needs to be stricter.

# Default owners for the whole repository.
*                       @felicabrera @Stefano936 @Luciavazquez01

# --- High risk areas ------------------------------------------------------
# Transparency log core: append-only guarantees, Merkle tree, checkpoints, and
# inclusion and consistency proof verification. A mistake here breaks the
# auditability of the entire system.
/internal/              @felicabrera @Stefano936 @Luciavazquez01
/cmd/                   @felicabrera @Stefano936 @Luciavazquez01

# Public audit website and verification CLI. This is where a user decides
# whether to trust a proof, so a display bug here is a security bug.
/web/                   @felicabrera @Stefano936 @Luciavazquez01

# Security, CI/CD and repository governance configuration.
